-- title:
--   Powers of mathfrak m_R lie in pⁿR
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and of characteristic zero, and let $p$ be a prime number whose image $(p:\mathcal O)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$ (so $\mathcal O$ has residue characteristic $p$). Let $R$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure such that $R$ is finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and suppose the structure map $\mathcal O \to R$ is a local homomorphism, i.e. it pulls the maximal ideal of $R$ back into the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Then for every natural number $n$ there exists a natural number $m$ such that $\mathfrak m_R^{\,m} \le (\,\mathrm{span}\,\{(p:R)\}\,)^n$, that is, the $m$-th power of the maximal ideal of $R$ is contained in the $n$-th power of the ideal of $R$ generated by $p$.
--
--   This is the standard comparison of the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic and $p$-adic filtrations on a module-finite local algebra over a discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $p$: the two topologies agree, so $\mathfrak m_R$-adic smallness forces congruences modulo powers of $p$. It is used in [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_quadraticRelation_forall_of_frobenius`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_quadraticRelation_forall_of_frobenius), where continuity of an adic Galois representation for the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic topology must be converted into statements modulo $p^n$.
